---
description: 'Pong implemented in Dart with Flutter'
import:
  - flutter-mobile-app-template
---

***definitions***

- :GameTitle: game title should be `Pong`.

***functional specs***

# game-view
The screen orientation is locked to landscape mode. :App: has a full-screen game view and its title is :GameTitle:.

# paddles
2 rectangles are drawn, one for each player. One on the left and one on the right side of the screen. Both paddles are inset from the screen edge by a finger's width (approximately 48 logical pixels) to avoid overlap with device notches and safe area insets.

# ball
A square ball starts in the center of the screen and starts moving in a random direction.
    - Random direction can be about 30deg up/down from horizon in both directions
    - The ball should bounce off the top and bottom edges of the screen
    - The ball should bounce off the player paddles
    - If the paddles are moving, add 60% of that movement to the ball's velocity to make it veer off from the perfect bounce.

# scoring
A scoring mechanism displays numbers at the top of the screen.
    - Score increases when the ball goes into the opponent's "goal" (off the screen on their side).

# game-modes
The game has two modes selectable from the start screen: "vs Computer" and "vs Player". Player 1 (left paddle) is always controlled by dragging a finger vertically on the left half of the screen; the paddle follows the finger's vertical position directly.
    - In "vs Computer" mode, Player 2 (right paddle) is controlled by the computer. The computer tracks the ball's vertical position and moves its paddle toward it at a speed slightly slower than the ball, so it is beatable. The computer paddle movement should have a small random reaction delay to feel natural.
    - In "vs Player" mode, Player 2 (right paddle) is controlled by a second human by tilting the phone forward and backward to move the paddle up and down.

# start-and-game-over-messages
At the beginning of the game, :App: shows mode selection buttons ("vs Computer" and "vs Player") together with instructions how to play the game. Tapping a mode button starts the game in that mode. When the game is over, :App: shows "You win! Tap to restart" or "Computer wins! Tap to restart" in "vs Computer" mode, or "Player 1 wins! Tap to restart" or "Player 2 wins! Tap to restart" in "vs Player" mode.

# restart-on-a-double-tap
A player can restart the game by double tapping the screen. When the player restarts the game, :App: shows a pop up message "Restart the game. Tap to restart".

# paddle-bounce-angle
The paddle acts like a reflective surface where the center produces a flat bounce, and hits above or below the center add upward or downward angle respectively, with a capped maximum angle.
